UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Collaborative data notebook and app-building platform with a built-in AI agent for SQL and Python. Community tier is free with limited features; Professional and Team plans are billed monthly per Editor seat, with GPU compute available as a separate pay-as-you-go add-on.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Hex is a collaborative data notebook and app-building platform that combines SQL and Python notebooks with AI-powered assistance, enabling analytics teams to build data analysis workflows and publish interactive apps from a single tool. Unlike traditional Jupyter notebooks, Hex is designed for team collaboration — multiple users can work in the same notebook simultaneously, with version control, sharing, and presentation built in.

Hex now leads with an AI agent, referred to on its pricing page as the Hex agent, which is available for trial even on the free Community plan and assists with SQL generation, Python code, chart configuration, and explaining queries. The platform connects to data warehouses including Snowflake, BigQuery, Databricks, and Redshift, and supports notebooks with mixed SQL/Python cells that share a data environment.

Key capabilities include collaborative SQL and Python notebooks, an AI agent for code generation and explanation, interactive app publishing, connections to major data warehouses, versioning, scheduling for automated notebook runs, and GPU compute for ML workloads billed by the hour.

Pricing: the Community tier is free and includes a Hex agent trial, connection to any data source, all cell types, small compute, up to three shared collections and components, and seven-day version history. The Professional plan is $36 per Editor per month, and the Team plan is $75 per Editor per month. Enterprise pricing is custom and includes an optional Explorer seat add-on. GPU compute is billed separately: A10G GPU at $4.06 per hour and L4 GPU at $2.93 per hour.

Limitations: Enterprise pricing requires contacting sales, which complicates upfront budget planning. GPU compute adds further variable cost on top of seat pricing. The Community free tier's small compute and limited shared collections make it best suited to individual trial use rather than full team rollout.

Best suited for analytics and data science teams at growth-stage and enterprise companies who want collaborative notebook tooling with AI assistance and the ability to publish interactive apps for business stakeholders.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET pros = ARRAY[$x$Real-time collaborative notebooks — multiple users simultaneously$x$, $x$Built-in Hex agent for AI-assisted SQL and Python generation and explanation, trialable on the free plan$x$, $x$Published apps let non-technical stakeholders interact with outputs without code access$x$, $x$Connects to Snowflake, BigQuery, Databricks, and Redshift$x$, $x$GPU compute available for ML workloads at published hourly rates (A10G $4.06/hr, L4 $2.93/hr)$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET cons = ARRAY[$x$Community free tier is limited to small compute and only three shared collections/components, suited to individual trial use rather than full team collaboration$x$, $x$Enterprise pricing is custom and requires contacting sales$x$, $x$GPU compute for ML workloads is billed separately by the hour, adding to total cost beyond seat pricing$x$, $x$Enterprise plans use an additional Explorer seat add-on separate from standard Editor seats, adding complexity to budgeting$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET choose_if = $x$["✅ You're a data scientist or analyst who wants collaborative Python and SQL notebooks with AI assistance", "✅ You build data apps — interactive tools where business users explore data with filters and inputs", "✅ You need a platform where data teams and business stakeholders can work in the same document", "✅ You want AI that writes SQL and Python from natural language and explains code"]$x$::jsonb
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET faq = $x$[{"q": "What is Hex?", "a": "Hex is a collaborative data platform combining SQL notebooks, Python, and no-code charts into a single workspace. Data teams use it to analyze data and build interactive data apps. The Hex agent writes SQL and Python from natural language, explains code, and auto-generates visualizations, and can be trialed on the free Community plan."}, {"q": "What is the difference between Looker Studio and Hex?", "a": "Looker Studio creates drag-and-drop visual dashboards — it's a reporting tool for business users. Hex is a data notebook and app builder for data teams who work in SQL and Python. Looker Studio is read-only visual reporting; Hex is interactive analysis and computation."}, {"q": "How much does Hex cost?", "a": "Hex offers a free Community plan with limited compute and shared collections. The Professional plan is $36 per Editor per month, and the Team plan is $75 per Editor per month. Enterprise pricing is custom and includes an optional Explorer seat add-on. GPU compute for ML workloads is billed separately by the hour."}]$x$::jsonb
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET best_for = $x$Cuadernos de datos y aplicaciones de IA colaborativos para equipos de analítica$x$
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'es';

UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Plataforma colaborativa de cuadernos de datos y creación de aplicaciones con un agente de IA integrado para SQL y Python. El nivel Community es gratuito con funciones limitadas; los planes Professional y Team se facturan mensualmente por puesto de Editor, con cómputo GPU disponible como complemento independiente de pago por uso.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'es';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Hex es una plataforma colaborativa de cuadernos de datos y creación de aplicaciones que combina cuadernos de SQL y Python con asistencia impulsada por IA, permitiendo a los equipos de analítica crear flujos de análisis de datos y publicar aplicaciones interactivas desde una sola herramienta. A diferencia de los cuadernos Jupyter tradicionales, Hex está diseñado para la colaboración en equipo: varios usuarios pueden trabajar en el mismo cuaderno simultáneamente, con control de versiones, compartición y presentación integrados.

Hex ahora se destaca por un agente de IA, denominado en su página de precios como el agente Hex, disponible para probar incluso en el plan gratuito Community, que ayuda con la generación de SQL, código Python, configuración de gráficos y explicación de consultas. La plataforma se conecta a almacenes de datos como Snowflake, BigQuery, Databricks y Redshift, y admite cuadernos con celdas mixtas de SQL/Python que comparten un entorno de datos.

Las capacidades clave incluyen cuadernos colaborativos de SQL y Python, un agente de IA para generación y explicación de código, publicación de aplicaciones interactivas, conexiones a los principales almacenes de datos, control de versiones, programación de ejecuciones automáticas de cuadernos y cómputo GPU para cargas de trabajo de ML facturado por hora.

Precios: el nivel Community es gratuito e incluye una prueba del agente Hex, conexión a cualquier fuente de datos, todos los tipos de celda, cómputo pequeño, hasta tres colecciones y componentes compartidos, y siete días de historial de versiones. El plan Professional cuesta 36 USD por Editor al mes, y el plan Team cuesta 75 USD por Editor al mes. El precio de Enterprise es personalizado e incluye un complemento opcional de puesto Explorer. El cómputo GPU se facturea por separado: GPU A10G a 4,06 USD por hora y GPU L4 a 2,93 USD por hora.

Limitaciones: el precio de Enterprise requiere contactar con ventas, lo que complica la planificación presupuestaria anticipada. El cómputo GPU añade un costo variable adicional sobre el precio por puesto. El cómputo pequeño y las colecciones compartidas limitadas del nivel gratuito Community lo hacen más adecuado para uso de prueba individual que para una implementación completa en equipo.

Es más adecuado para equipos de analítica y ciencia de datos en empresas en etapa de crecimiento y grandes empresas que desean herramientas de cuadernos colaborativos con asistencia de IA y la capacidad de publicar aplicaciones interactivas para partes interesadas del negocio.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'hex' AND lang = 'es';

